\par
{$B$}, it is possible to predict the expected reduction in standard
\par
{$A$}
\par
error of {$\DeltaCd$}
\par
, which is then followed through to a predicted reduction in standard error of
\par
{$\Delta$}B (i.e. reduction in decision uncertainty, Figure 2). The EVSI and the ENGS of the proposed
\par
study can then be calculated. This approach is repeated with combinations of sample sizes
\par
for observations on {$\DeltaCd$}
\par
{$A$} and {$\DeltaCd$}
\par
{$B$}. The ENGS-maximising combination is the optimal
\par
combination. (Note that we assume that only one process is observed in each individual.
\par
This is a limitation of the method and is considered in the discussion.)
\par
