\par
This explanation comprises three sections. In the first, the basic model is set up linking prior
\par
data or expert beliefs explicitly to distributions of incremental net benefit and its
\par
components. The second section explains the relationship between the two data collection
\par
processes for the incremental cost of drugs. The final section briefly explains how the value
\par
of information statistics are calculated; more detailed explanations of these are available
\par
elsewhere e.g. (18, 25).
