122.4 Data
\par
Full details are provided in Appendix 1. Briefly, data are taken from a study of 359 patients
\par
randomised to leukotriene receptor antagonists versus conventional treatment in asthma
\par
patients in a UK setting (the `ELEVATE' study).(28, 29) The data were divided into drug and
\par
NHS-non drug costs and QALYs gained at two years. For illustrative purposes, {$\Delta$}B was
\par
calculated at a threshold of \pounds 5000 per QALY.
\par
Drug costs were originally calculated in a bottom-up manner at individual preparation level,
\par
based on actual quantities of drugs prescribed. To simulate a `top down' approach, the cost
\par
for each datum was recalculated at the BNF chapter section level, using aggregate cost per
\par
prescription as reported in the Prescription Cost Analysis 2005.(30) Therefore every patient
\par
had two estimates of drug costs, one based on actual prescribed doses of drugs and the
\par
other an approximation aggregated at the BNF section level. We define process A as the
\par
drug costs estimated using actual prescribed doses, and process B as the approximation
\par
aggregated at BNF section level.
\par
The resulting summary statistics are in Tables ‎ 1-
\par
‎ 2. At a willingness to pay for a QALY of
\par
\pounds 5000 and using process A for drug costs, incremental net benefit is \pounds 56.41. The adoption
\par
decision would therefore be in favour of intervention.
\par
As process `A' is considered superior to `B', estimates of mean {$\Delta$}B are based on data from
\par
process A. Nevertheless, for the purpose of illustration, recalculating the results using
\par
process B yields an incremental net benefit of -\pounds 130.86. Using these data the adoption
\par
decision would be in favour of control (Table 1).
\par
The population who could benefit from the information is 524,380 (Appendix 1). The fixed
\par
cost of sampling is \pounds 1,305,470, with a variable cost of \pounds 288.58 per patient to collect all data
\par
components (QALYs, non-drug and drug costs, Appendix 1). We assume a per patient
\par
variable cost of \pounds 192.19 for a trial collecting solely QALY or cost data (2/3rds the full cost),
\par
\pounds 96.19 for one collecting data on either non-drug cost or drug cost data alone (1/3rd) and
\par
\pounds 9.62 for one collecting only drug cost data using process B (1/10th the cost of process A).
\par
These costs are assumptions based on the authors' opinions and experience as to the
\par
relative research effort required to collect and analyse the data.
