\par
7. Conclusions
\par
Large scale multi-sensor fusion is a very important issue in future networks and internet of things,
\par
especially in the domains of disaster response and military operations. However, previous centralized
\par
data aggregation algorithms for small sensor network are no longer feasible in considering of huge
\par
network expenses as well as the energy expenses for central nodes. In this paper, we have proposed
\par
an extremely economic data relay algorithm that sensors could proactively make broadcast decisions
\par
by neat matrix computation to balance transmission and save energy. By encoding sensors' local
\par
knowledge to three matrixes: network connection, data distribution and data utility matrix, they can
\par
do the reasoning for all the pending data by only a neat matrix computation. We also built heuristic
\par
algorithms for sensors to well maintain those matrixes with only a local view to the network so that
\par
this design can be adaptive to the scalable and dynamic environment. Our experimental simulations
\par
manifested that our approach is scalable and effectively balance between promoting data fusion
\par
process and saving energy to prolong the life time of the whole network.
