Modeling procedure
\par
Underlying regularities are found from the learning
\par
knowledge base which consists of known fault types,
\par
sensor monitoring data, and historical records. Fault
\par
diagnostics can be performed by the DBN by extracting
\par
this information. The proposed SIF-based diagnostic
\par
model is shown in Figure 2. The modeling procedure is
\par
described in the following steps.
\par
Step 1: obtain the mutual information and synergy
\par
coefficient. For the diagnosed system, the mutual infor-
\par
mation of all pairs of sensors and individual sensors
\par
with respect to Y are computed. The synergy coeffi-
\par
cient is defined as the measure of the expected syner-
\par
getic potential between sensors Si and Sj in reducing
\par
the uncertainty of situation Y, so it follows that
