\par
Abstract The current study involved methodology and
\par
content analyses of abstracts of 30 clinical decision support
\par
system (CDSS) related studies with high impact factors.
\par
The main aim of the current work was to identify the
\par
performance and efficiency of CDSS, and enhance the
\par
understanding of CDSS for a better health management
\par
among the physicians and the patients. To add structure to
\par
the current study, major research areas were categorized
\par
based on a multidimensional unfolding analysis. In this
\par
regard, eight studies were conducted based on theoretical
\par
research, ten studies were related to the system and per-
\par
formance of CDSS, and 12 studies verified the efficacy
\par
through analysis and evaluation of CDSS. The results
\par
indicated that the above-mentioned studies on improve-
\par
ment in systematic performance. Then, based on the im-
\par
provement, effectively used evaluations were conducted
\par
comparably. Moreover, 14 studies analyzed patients' data
\par
and assessed decision support system (DSS). The related
\par
findings denoted that DSS has been mainly used for patient
\par
management and a large number of studies have verified its
\par
effectiveness, using several data to ensure its accuracy and
\par
reliability. In addition, the analyzed results of the abstracts
\par
and the titles were compared to find whether the titles of
\par
the literature articles reveal their content. Using these
\par
methodological studies, the academic outlook of medical
\par
informatics could be forecasted and the academic quality
\par
could be improved by resolving the problems, arising out
\par
of system development and realization processes. Such
\par
problems can be solved through analyses and interpretation
\par
of multilateral parameters, such as the trend in academic
\par
development, research direction, topics and methods.
\par
Keywords Decision support Clinical decision support
\par
system Expert system Knowledge system Medical
\par
knowledge
