4. Analysis
\par
The manufacturer acts as the leader by announcing its wholesale price, online price, and cooperative advertising expenditure first. The retailer
\par
then acts as the follower by announcing its retail price, knowing the manufacturer's decisions. In order to prevent the retailer from buying the man-
\par
ufacturer's product through the online channel for a lower price, we assume that the manufacturer's wholesale price w is not higher than its online
\par
price p1, that is, w {$\leq$} p1. For the Stackelberg game, we first examine the value of the manufacturer's cooperative advertising under the two settings:
\par
(1) the non-information sharing and (2) the information sharing. We then develop valuable strategies for business managers.
\par
