Appendix 3
\par
716 5. Conclusions and managerial implications
\par
In this paper, we assumed a manufacturer--retailer supply chain
\par
where the manufacturer opens an online channel to compete with its
\par
retailer and provides a monetary support to the retailer to implement
\par
a local advertising campaign. Both the manufacturer and the retailer
\par
have private information about the market demand. We thus examine
\par
the value of manufacturer's cooperative advertising and its strategic in-
\par
fluence on information sharing of the supply chain players. Our results
\par
show that the manufacturer's cooperative advertising coordinates the
\par
dual-channel distributions effectively and helps improve the channel
\par
performance under the environment of demand uncertainty. However,
\par
the manufacturer's cooperative advertising also stimulates the retailer
\par
to distort its information while the manufacturer has a motivation
\par
to understate its forecast. The information distortion may make
\par
the shared information useless or even stop information from being
\par
shared between firms. We thus propose that the manufacturer and
\par
the retailer employ an advertising agency to verify their shared informa-
\par
tion and help make an optimal investment in advertising, so that
\par
information distortion can be eliminated and optimum results can be
\par
achieved.
\par
Our research addresses important issues and our findings provide
\par
valuable managerial implications for business managers. The most sig-
\par
nificant contribution is that our paper contributes to the substantial
\par
and growing research about the value of manufacturer's cooperative
\par
advertising in a manufacturer--retailer dual-channel distribution with
\par
information issues. When e-commerce is becoming more and more
\par
popular in the business market, many manufacturers would like to use
\par
online and traditional channels to sell their products directly to
\par
consumers. Thus, it is managerially important to develop some valuable
