1. Introduction
\par
Based on global experiences, integrated watershed management is the key to solving
\par
watershed pollution problems. In the USA, Canada, Australia, and other developed
\par
countries, water quality goals and standards have more speci c requirements within
\par
administrative boundaries and are included in the overall watershed management frame-
\par
work (Daniel, Pinel, \& Brooks, 2013; Giri, Nejadhashemi, \& Woznicki, 2012; Hassanzadeh,
\par
Elshorbagy, Gober, \& Wheater, 2014; Millington \& Ongley, 2003). Most developed countries
\par
have strict environmental laws and legal systems that rigorously manage pollution
\par
