2.5.2 Dependent basic random variables
\par
Eqs. (7-9) must be adjusted when dependence among the {$X$}! 's is present, in accordance with
\par
the case-specific BN structure. However, the principles outlined above for independent
\par
{$X$}!, \dots{} , {$X$}! hold equally for dependent basic random variables: The discretization error is a
\par
function of the cells cut by the limit state function.
\par
When determining an optimal discretization, we propose in the following to find the FORM
\par
approximation of the reliability problem, which can readily account for the dependence
\par
among the random variables. Hence, there is no need to distinguish between cases with
\par
independent or dependent random variables.
